{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "וישתחו לך", :translit "veyishtachavu lekha", :gloss "and they shall bow to you"} {:he "חסר וי\"ו", :translit "chaser vav", :gloss "defective vav"} {:he "ו' דורות", :translit "v'dorot", :gloss "six generations"} {:he "שמדוד עד יורם", :translit "sheh-mi-david ad yoram", :gloss "from David until Joram"} {:he "שעבדו אדום את ישראל", :translit "she-avadu edom et yisra'el", :gloss "that Edom enslaved Israel"} {:he "ומכאן ואילך פשע בו", :translit "u-mikan va-eilach pasha bo", :gloss "and from here onward he transgressed against him"} {:he "כ\"ו תיבות", :translit "kated-tav teivot", :gloss "twenty-six words"} {:he "בשם הנכבד שעולה כ\"ו", :translit "beshem ha-nikhbad she-oleh kated-vav", :gloss "with the honored Name whose value is twenty-six"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "ו'", :b "חסר וי\"ו"} {:kind :masorah, :count 26, :occurrences ["כ\"ו תיבות"]} {:kind :other, :note "Twenty-six words in the blessing correspond to the Tetragrammaton's gematria."}], :frame {:text "The House of David ruled for six generations — David, Solomon, Rehoboam, Abijah, Asa, Jehoshaphat — until Jehoshaphat's son Joram, during whose reign Edom revolted from Judah's rule, as recorded at 2 Kings 8:20–22. The word וישתחו is written with a defective vav, and Ba'al HaTurim reads the missing letter as hinting to those six generations of Davidic dominion over Esau's descendants before Edom broke free. The Tetragrammaton has the numerical value of twenty-six.", :sources ["2 Kings 8:20–22"]}} {:quotes [{:he "הוה", :translit "haveh", :gloss "be"} {:he "הוה גביר לאחיך", :translit "haveh gavir le'akheikha", :gloss "be a lord to your brother"} {:he "כי לשלג יאמר הוה ארץ", :translit "ki le-sheleg yo-mar haveh eretz", :gloss "for to the snow he says: be earth"} {:he "בזכות יעקב יורד גשם ושלג", :translit "b-z'chut ya'akov yored geshem u-sheleg", :gloss "in the merit of Jacob rain and snow descend"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["הוה גביר לאחיך" "כי לשלג יאמר הוה ארץ"]}], :frame {:text "Job 37:6 reads כִּי לַשֶׁלֶג יֹאמַר הֱוֵא אָרֶץ ('for to the snow He says: Be, earth'), where God commands snow to cover the earth. Ba'al HaTurim links the word הוה in Isaac's blessing 'be a lord to your brother' (Genesis 27:29) with the identical word in Job 37:6, teaching that in the merit of Jacob — to whom the blessing of dominion was given — both rain and snow descend upon the earth.", :sources ["Job 37:6" "Genesis 27:29"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :gematria, :a "ו'", :a-value 6, :b "חסר וי\"ו", :b-value 290, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false} {:kind :masorah, :count 26, :occurrences ["כ\"ו תיבות"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "כ\"ו תיבות", :refs [], :n 0, :lens :plene-insensitive}]} {:kind :other, :note "Twenty-six words in the blessing correspond to the Tetragrammaton's gematria.", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["הוה גביר לאחיך" "כי לשלג יאמר הוה ארץ"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "הוה גביר לאחיך", :refs ["Genesis 27:29"], :n 1, :lens :exact} {:phrase "כי לשלג יאמר הוה ארץ", :refs [], :n 0, :lens :plene-insensitive}]}], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:08:47.813132119Z", :model "glm-5.2"}